<section class="we-opening">
  <div class="we-opening-inner">
    <div class="we-eyebrow">You know this moment</div>
    <h2 class="we-opening-head">
      The conversation stalls —<br />
      and more words <em>won't move it.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="we-opening-body">
      If you hold space for other people — in a practice, a classroom, a
      session room, a team — you know the moment. The story has been told
      twice. The insight is accurate, and it changes nothing. Something in the
      room is asking for a language that words can't offer.
    </p>
    <p class="we-opening-body">
      This masterclass is about exactly that moment. In Somatic Vocal Healing
      the question isn't <em>tell me more about it</em> — it's <em>what is the
      sound of it?</em> Sound before story: one honest tone can carry what
      would take ten careful minutes to circle in words, and the person in
      front of you was born knowing how to make it.
    </p>
    <p class="we-opening-body">
      Not a replacement for your training. Something that sits underneath it —
      a way to let the body speak when the mind has run out of road.
    </p>
    <p class="we-opening-accent">
      "I've never had a therapist ask me: <em>could you make a sound for
      that?</em> It's odd and sad that it doesn't happen — because it's still
      so natural to us." — Jacob
    </p>
    <p class="we-opening-pull">
      Talking circles it.<br />Sounding enters it.
    </p>
    <a href="#register" class="we-link-cta">
      Reserve your seat <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right"></i>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
